# MeedyaSuite-core — Project Brief

## What Is This?

MeedyaSuite-core is the shared Rust core library for the MeedyaSuite product family.
It eliminates code duplication across MeedyaDL, MeedyaConverter, MeedyaManager, and
MeedyaDB by providing canonical type definitions and shared business logic.

## The Problem It Solves

Before this library, three active projects independently maintained:
- Audio/video codec enums (42+ audio codecs, 21+ video codecs)
- Container format definitions (36+ formats with extensions, MIME types)
- Metadata tag registries (TOML/JSON5-driven freeform atom definitions)
- Audio fingerprinting (AcoustID/Chromaprint)
- ReplayGain loudness analysis (EBU R128)
- MeedyaDB API client code
- Metadata provider integrations (MusicBrainz, TMDB, TheTVDB, etc.)
- DJ metadata (BPM, key, cue points, Mixed In Key analysis)
- Lyrics fetch/parse/write and library import (iTunes XML, CUE sheets)

This duplication existed across Rust (MeedyaDL, MeedyaManager) and Swift
(MeedyaConverter), making changes error-prone and inconsistent.

## Crate Responsibilities

The workspace is 9 crates. See [`README.md`](../README.md)'s crate table for the
authoritative, current list (purpose, implementation status, per-crate test count) — it is
not repeated here so this brief cannot drift out of sync with it.

### meedya-codecs (Priority 1 — highest value)
The single source of truth for codec identity. Defines AudioCodec, VideoCodec,
SubtitleCodec, ContainerFormat, HdrFormat, SpatialAudioFormat enums with rich
metadata (FFmpeg names, lossless flags, compatibility matrices, classification).

### meedya-metadata (Priority 2)
Config-driven metadata tag system. TagRegistry loads tag definitions from TOML
(zero code changes to add tags). JSON path extraction engine for API responses.
CommonTag enum mapping standard field names across iTunes atoms, Vorbis Comments,
and ID3v2 frames. Also owns the cross-repo `identifier_types` registry and a
filename `template` engine shared across the downstream apps.

### meedya-tags-extended
Multi-format (lofty-based) DJ metadata foundation: BPM/key/cue points/loops/beat
grid, plus a Mixed In Key reader. Other proprietary DJ readers (Serato, Rekordbox,
Traktor, Virtual DJ) are pending fixture-based implementation sessions.

### meedya-library-import
Ingests playback bounds and metadata from external library databases — iTunes /
Music.app XML and CUE sheets — into a normalized `LibraryEntry` stream.

### meedya-lyrics
LRCLIB client, LRC parser/writer, sidecar + tag-embed writes (plain text and
synced ID3v2 SYLT), plus the `.lyrics` YAML canonical model with Apple Music TTML
import and multi-format export.

### meedya-fingerprint (Priority 3)
Audio identification and loudness analysis. AcoustID API client with rate limiting.
ReplayGain analyzer using FFmpeg EBU R128 filter. Returns results only — consumers
handle tag writing via meedya-metadata. Fingerprint *generation* (Chromaprint) is
behind a non-default, opt-in Cargo feature.

### meedya-providers
Centralised metadata provider framework. `MetadataProvider` trait, capabilities
system, rate limiting, credential storage, cover art helpers, match scoring, and
in-repo provider implementations (feature-gated, one per external service) —
MusicBrainz, Spotify, Apple Music, Deezer, TMDb, TheTVDB, OMDb, Apple TV, iTunes
Store, Apple Podcasts, ISRC, EIDR, ISWC.

### meedya-db (Priority 4)
Shared media record types (Track, Album, Artist). MeedyaDB API client for
api.meedya.tv/v1. DbExporter trait for multi-backend database export.

### meedya-core
Unified facade crate re-exporting all of the above behind Cargo feature flags, so
a downstream app can depend on one crate instead of nine.

## Integration Status

| Consumer | Status | Integration Path |
|----------|--------|-----------------|
| MeedyaDL (Rust/Tauri) | Pending | Direct Cargo git dependency |
| MeedyaManager (Rust) | Pending | Direct Cargo git dependency |
| MeedyaConverter (Swift) | Pending | Via bindings/swift C FFI (not yet scaffolded) |
| MeedyaDB (Swift) | Not started | Via bindings/swift C FFI (not yet scaffolded) |

## Key Dependencies

- serde (serialization), toml + serde_yaml (config / YAML), thiserror (errors), strum (enum derive)
- reqwest + tokio (HTTP/async for API clients), governor (rate limiting)
- lofty (multi-format tag I/O — one of the two co-existing tag-I/O surfaces)
- quick-xml (TTML/XML parsing in meedya-lyrics)
- rusty-chromaprint + symphonia (pure-Rust fingerprinting — behind the opt-in `chromaprint` feature on meedya-fingerprint)
- chrono (timestamps), serde_json (JSON handling)

MSRV: Rust 1.82 (declared via `rust-version`; driven by `Option::is_none_or`).

## Testing

See [`README.md`](../README.md) for the current total test count and per-crate
breakdown — deliberately not repeated here. This repo's chronic failure mode is
doc-count drift across multiple files; a single source of truth avoids it.
Run with `cargo test --workspace` (or `--all-features` for the CI configuration).
All tests must pass before any push.
